  {
   "k": "1ibkp4j",
   "en": "In December 1911, after ⟦0⟧ declared independence, the Qing vassal state of Tannu Uriankhai became the independent Uriankhay Republic. The new republic was unstable, as many Tuvans preferred joining ⟦1⟧ over remaining independent. Fearing Chinese occupation, ⟦2⟧ joined Russia as an autonomous Protectorate in April of 1914. In 1918, chaos erupted as ⟦3⟧ invaded during the outbreak of the Russian Civil War. Between 1918 and 1921, Tuva became a warzone contested by the ⟦4⟧ and ⟦5⟧.",
   "frags": 6
  },
